  "explains": "InvoiceService.total in InvoiceService.java multiplies by 120 instead of 100. Who uses the file: InvoiceController imports the class and spells total in its handler total (format(service.total(id))), so that handler is reached and its route is GET /ledger/v1/invoices/{id}/total: the context path /ledger of application.properties, the class mapping Paths.INVOICES (a constant of Paths: BASE plus /invoices), the method mapping /{id}/total. The other handlers of the controller never spell total, so their routes are not reached. AuditController imports InvoiceService too but spells only list: it is excluded by narrowing with its import line and the class that changed. Docs.java names InvoiceService#total in a comment and in a string, which is not code: it is no importer. InvoiceServiceTest uses the class from the same package with no import and InvoiceControllerTest imports it: both are unit tests, not callers. The route is called by the web client through fetchTotal, and that is followed to the screen /invoices/:invoiceId (the screen /invoices does not call fetchTotal).",
